@0    = ~Okay, but cats are better than dogs because--~
@1    = ~Faren. I wanted a word with you. What are you trying to play at with <CHARNAME>? I hardly think you've been acting appropriately.~
@2    = ~Who the hell told you to barge in?~
@3    = ~I'm not barging in, I'm trying to say that you're putting us in danger. You're distracting <CHARNAME>, and you're distracting me. We could be attacked any moment and you're talking about - about ridiculous things like this!~
@4    = ~That's the point. Okay, we could be attacked, but when we're not, we have to keep our spirits up. Something you're in dire need of.~
@5    = ~What's that supposed to mean?~
@6    = ~No, never mind. If you want to carry on being - being frivolous, go on. I'll be keeping my eyes open for trouble.~
@7    = ~Look, I think we all know Nathaniel has a huge crush on you, and I'm fine with that, but--~
@8    = ~What? I don't, <CHARNAME> - that is, I--~
@9    = ~Normally I'd be fine with you going with me on the side, but stringing both of us along isn't fair on him. So, what's it to be?~
@10   = ~I don't know what you're talking about, Faren.~
@11   = ~Personally, I prefer Nathaniel's company to yours, Faren.~
@12   = ~I'm all yours, Faren. I don't want you to feel like I'm using you.~
@13   = ~You mean you haven't noticed him checking you out every second of the <DAYNIGHT>? If you hadn't, you'd have to be - well - as dumb as he is.~
@14   = ~Excuse me?!~
@15   = ~Figuratively speaking. Er, well, now you do know, what do you want to do?~
@16   = ~Back off, Faren. I'll do what I want, and I like Nathaniel more than you.~
@17   = ~I see what you mean. I consider you a friend, but nothing more.~
@18   = ~I should hope so! <CHARNAME>, this man's just a nuisance. I don't know why you keep him around.~
@19   = ~...well. That's kind of taken the wind out of my sails. I wasn't expecting you to say that.~
@20   = ~But fair enough, if you want that I can't exactly order you around.~
@21   = ~...well. I thought you enjoyed talking to me, <CHARNAME>, but obviously not. I won't bother you in the future.~
@22   = ~Good to know, <CHARNAME>. Thanks for clearing that up.~
@23   = ~Here. You dropped a bit of your lunch.~
@24   = ~Oh - thanks. Wouldn't want to go hungry, now would I?~
@25   = ~Okay, don't answer, then. Nathaniel, seriously. Do you have to glare at me quite this much? It's getting annoying - and, to be honest, kind of hurtful.~
@26   = ~I'm not glaring. I just gave you your food, didn't I?~
@27   = ~But you keep giving me these dark looks like you think <CHARNAME>'s an idiot for dragging me around. I know I'm not some hotshot trained guardsman, but I am useful.~
@28   = ~That's not the point.~
@29   = ~I kind of think it is.~
@30   = ~No, it's-- oh, don't worry about it. I'm sorry.~
@31   = ~Did your friend - Jessalyn, isn't it? - did she have formal training?~
@32   = ~Sort of. She was in some sort of retreat up in the mountains when she was little, but she left when she was fifteen and realised she wanted to be rebellious.~
@33   = ~Heh, never seen anyone so fast on their feet as she was. And she and Araden...they'd always be clowning around.~
@34   = ~That sounds like my friend Fiona. She's always messing around with Kennedy. But she's a very good fighter. I saw her knock out three pirates in a couple of seconds, once.~
@35   = ~Now she sounds like my kind of girl. Can you introduce us?~
@36   = ~Oh - no, she's not - I mean, she likes women.~
@37   = ~Damn, the best ones always do.~
@38   = ~It sounds like adventuring really got you back on the rails. I'm glad it ended up that way.~
@39   = ~Me, too. I'd have hated hanging around Athkatla any longer, getting into fights.~
@40   = ~Do...you think you would have gone travelling if you hadn't had your friends around?~
@41   = ~No way. I never really told them how much of a difference they made - not when I was sober, anyway.~
@42   = ~I see. Thank you.~
@43   = ~Oh, I get it. Is this about your boyfriend? Because, to be honest, it sounds like he would do whatever he wanted whether he had friends around or not.~
@44   = ~You're...probably right.~
@45   = ~Of course I'm right. You want to spar?~
@46   = ~Okay.~
@47   = ~You're leaving your side open, there. And move your leg back, you're putting your weight wrong...~
